This is Omni View Top World News, episode 17. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Alabama, Florida, and Mississippi have declared states of emergency as the storm closes on the Gulf. The National Hurricane Center says it should come ashore Friday night near the Alabama Florida line, with surge up to seven feet and waves as high as 30 feet. At daybreak, the winds were 105 miles an hour, the Guardian reports.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:35.100
and by mid-morning, the center sat about 145 miles southeast of the Mississippi River mouth,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:41.000
moving north-northeast at 15 miles an hour. Noah expects hurricane force winds over the Florida

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.220
Panhandle, Southern Alabama and Southern Mississippi, and says people there should get ready for long

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:52.660
power cuts. Surges forecast from Southeast Louisiana to Suwani and Northeast Florida, with as much as 15

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:57.960
inches of rain and tornadoes possible overnight into Saturday from Alabama across the Panhandle into

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.560
to southwest Georgia. The center flagged a seven-foot surge risk at Dauphin Island and

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.860
six feet at Indian pass and said preparation should be finished fast. In Beijing, after

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:12.380
two days of talks, China and the European Union reached preliminary agreements on hybrid

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:18.480
cars, market access, and rare earths. EU reporter says. Trade Commissioner Maro Schaeff-Tavitch

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:23.260
says there is a shared understanding to moderate Chinese hybrid and plug-in shipments, with

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:27.860
the aim of cutting those exports to the EU by more than half over four years. He said

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.040
But this is the first time China has accepted export moderation without a prior trade fight.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.280
The mechanism is still undisclosed, and EU leaders must endorse it in Brussels next Thursday,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.300
ahead of the European Council Summit.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.920
They also share an understanding on easing rare earth and permanent magnet exports through

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.300
a fast-track licensing system already in place.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:52.200
Teraf cuts would cover EU goods from car parts to olive oil and footwear, almost 4 billion euros

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.160
of current exports, with duty savings estimated at least 225 million euros.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:01.100
Shaf Chavitch called the deficit unsustainable, and the step limited.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.340
ACES, Sigurd DeVries welcomed it as a way to manage China's place in the European market

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.340
