00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.160
Unemployment edged up one-tenth of a point to 6.5%.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:10.020
Education lost 35,300 jobs, health care and social assistance 23,100, manufacturing 12,700,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.780
while professional and technical services added 10,600.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:21.880
Quebec lost 49,000, Ontario and British Columbia 20,000 each, and Alberta added 23,000. Full-time

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:28.660
work fell by 35,000 and part-time by 33,000. Youth employment dropped 48,000. The blog

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:34.760
says the Bank of Canada is likely to hold its policy rate at 2.25% in October, with a quarter-point

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:40.240
